---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const aboutPhoto = "/images/about/matteo-curcio-dubai-camera.jpg";
const aboutAnimated = "/media/about.mp4";
const aboutAnimatedFallback = aboutPhoto;

const pathways = [
  {
    href: "/services/",
    label: "Services",
    note: "Finishing, workflow, coaching, and the infrastructure side of delivery."
  },
  {
    href: "/workflow/#secure-systems",
    label: "Cybersecurity",
    note: "Creative systems now depend on trust, access, automation, and data. This is the security angle behind the workflow work."
  },
  {
    href: "/reels/music/",
    label: "Music",
    note: "I come from music production, and everything I make still has to move with rhythm: edits, grades, decks, systems."
  },
  {
    href: "/blog/",
    label: "Writing",
    note: "Field notes, workflow pieces, and technical writing from real projects."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Melbourne Colourist & Online Editor | Matteo Curcio"
  description="Matteo Curcio is a Melbourne-based freelance colourist, online editor and finishing artist, working across post-production, infrastructure and music."
  path="/about"
>
  <article class="prose about-page">
    <header class="about-intro">
      <h1>A colourist and online editor, by way of some useful detours.</h1>
      <p class="about-lead">
        I grade, conform and finish commercial and branded work in Melbourne. Before that I worked in IT, in music
        production and on large event productions in Dubai, and all three still show up in the work: I read a brief
        like a producer, a timeline like a musician and a delivery spec like a sysadmin.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="about-story-block">
      <div class="about-story-copy">
        <p>
          It started in Milan in 1997. I worked as a sysadmin and developer while studying jazz and electronic
          music, and volunteered with the Italian Red Cross. Then I swapped servers for studios: audio engineering,
          music production, and Musetta, the duo I co-founded. We made records, played internationally, and one of
          our tracks ended up on Better Call Saul, which is still the quickest way to explain my music career at
          a dinner party.
        </p>

        <p>
          Next came Dubai, and several years of large-scale events and experiential productions across the region,
          including projects for Dubai Tourism and Expo 2020. I also filmed 360° video in a refugee camp near the
          Syrian border.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-story-block">
      <div class="about-story-copy">
        <figure class="about-inline-media about-photo-frame">
          <img src={aboutPhoto} alt="Matteo Curcio operating a camera rig in Abu Dhabi" loading="eager" />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-story-block">
      <div class="about-story-copy">
        <p>
          In Melbourne I moved into colour grading and broadcast finishing, which turned out to use everything that
          came before: the ear for rhythm, the eye for a system, and the patience for a fifth round of notes. More
          recently I added a cybersecurity qualification, so it’s now official that I never really left IT.
        </p>

        <p>
          I also coach Adobe Creative Cloud at RMIT’s Adobe Hub, where the job is getting people past which button
          to press and on to why it works.
        </p>

        <p>
          Put me in a grading suite, a machine room or a production meeting and I’ll find something useful to do
          in each: colour science, signal paths, media workflows, or the thing that worked perfectly yesterday and
          has decided not to today.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-story-block">
      <div class="about-story-copy">
        <figure class="about-inline-media about-animated-frame">
          <video autoplay loop muted playsinline preload="metadata" poster={aboutAnimatedFallback} aria-label="Animated behind-the-scenes clip from Matteo Curcio's About page">
            <source src={aboutAnimated} type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-story-block">
      <div class="about-story-copy">
        <p>
          Outside work, I play bass, make music and run two podcasts: Musica Arcana, about the hidden systems,
          encoded meanings and ritual functions buried in music; and Italian Music Pioneers, about a century
          of Italian musicians who refused to behave.
        </p>

        <p>
          I shoot black-and-white street photography, cook risotto, and keep adding pages to a cookbook
          currently scheduled for release in 2054. I also run an unnecessarily elaborate homelab, 3D-print
          solutions to problems that probably did not require custom manufacturing, and occasionally spend
          more time researching how an object was designed than a reasonable person would spend using it.
        </p>

        <p>
          My real hobby may simply be reducing uncertainty from 4.7% to 3.9%.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <nav class="about-pathways" aria-label="About page links">
      {pathways.map((item) => (
        <a class="about-pathway" href={item.href}>
          <span class="about-pathway-label">{item.label}</span>
          <span class="about-pathway-note">{item.note}</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
